# English-only project language

NeuroCut is an English-first open-source repository.

## Required

- Write **all** new and edited source code comments, docstrings, UI strings, commit messages, CI config comments, and documentation in **English**.
- Do not add Cyrillic text or Russian-language product copy to the repo.
- Prefer English terms in user-facing UI (`brief` instead of `ТЗ`, `clip` instead of `ролик`, etc.).

## Allowed exceptions

- Upstream artifact names and paths that cannot be renamed (e.g. `gigaam-ru/`, vendor archive URLs).
- ISO language codes used as technical values (`ru`, `en`) in STT routing or config — without Russian prose around them.
- Content inside user-uploaded media / transcripts at runtime (not committed).

## When editing

If you touch a file that still contains non-English project prose, translate it to English in the same change when practical.
